---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ExamResizer from '../components/ExamResizer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="IBPS Photo, Signature, Thumb & Declaration Resizer (2026 Free) — PdfAndImg"
  description="Free 4-in-1 IBPS image resizer for PO, Clerk, and RRB. Convert candidate photo (20-50KB), signature (10-20KB), left thumb (20-50KB), and handwritten declaration (50-100KB) in your browser."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-24" style="max-width: 1000px;">
    
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div style="display: inline-block; padding: 6px 16px; background: rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.3); border-radius: 100px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-lime); margin-bottom: 16px;">
        IBPS / SBI / RRB READY
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 16px; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1;">
        IBPS 4-in-1 <span style="color: var(--color-lime);">Photo, Signature &amp; Document Resizer</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--color-ink-2); max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.6;">
        Instantly format all 4 required IBPS &amp; SBI portal documents: Photograph (20–50KB), Signature (10–20KB), Left Thumb Impression (20–50KB), and Handwritten Declaration (50–100KB).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The Exam Resizer Component -->
    <ExamResizer defaultExam="ibps" defaultType="photo" allowMultiple={true} />

    <!-- SEO Content Section -->
    <article style="margin-top: 80px; padding-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); font-family: var(--font-body); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-2);">
      
      <h2 style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 24px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2;">The Ultimate Guide to IBPS Photo & Signature Resize (2026-2027 Exam Cycle)</h2>
      
      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: 1.125rem;">
        Applying for the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection (IBPS) exams—whether it's for PO, Clerk, Specialist Officer (SO), or RRB—requires strict adherence to their digital upload guidelines. The application portal is notorious for rejecting images that are even slightly off the required dimensions or file size limits. A single error in your photo or signature upload can disqualify your entire application.
      </p>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-2); padding: 32px; border-radius: 16px; margin-bottom: 40px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 24px;">Exact 4-in-1 IBPS Document Specifications (Official Guidelines)</h3>
        
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 32px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));">
          <div>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><polyline points="21 15 16 10 5 21"/></svg>
              1. Candidate Photograph
            </strong>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>File Size:</strong> Strictly 20 KB to 50 KB</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 200 x 230 pixels</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Format:</strong> .JPG or .JPEG only</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Background:</strong> Plain white or light-colored background</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"/></svg>
              2. Candidate Signature
            </strong>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>File Size:</strong> Strictly 10 KB to 20 KB</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 140 x 60 pixels</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Ink:</strong> Black ink pen on white paper</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: #ef4444;">✗</span> <span style="color: #ef4444;"><strong>Warning:</strong> Block / Capital letters are rejected.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3zM7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3"/></svg>
              3. Left Thumb Impression (LTI)
            </strong>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>File Size:</strong> Strictly 20 KB to 50 KB</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 240 x 240 pixels (3cm × 3cm)</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Ink:</strong> Blue or Black ink stamp on white paper</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Clarity:</strong> Ensure ridges are clearly defined and unsmudged</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-lime)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
              4. Handwritten Declaration
            </strong>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>File Size:</strong> Strictly 50 KB to 100 KB</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 800 x 400 pixels (10cm × 5cm)</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: var(--color-lime);">✓</span> <span><strong>Ink:</strong> Written in candidate's own hand with Black ink</span></li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 8px;"><span style="color: #ef4444;">✗</span> <span style="color: #ef4444;"><strong>Warning:</strong> In English only. Capital letters prohibited.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 16px;">Step-by-Step: How to Resize Photo for IBPS PO, Clerk & SO</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Preparing your files correctly is half the battle won during the busy IBPS application season. Here is the foolproof process to format your documents:</p>
      
      <ol style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
        <li><strong>Capture the Perfect Shot:</strong> Sit facing a window or under bright natural light. Ensure your background is a plain white wall. Do not wear heavy makeup, reflective glasses, or face coverings.</li>
        <li><strong>Scan or Photograph Your Signature:</strong> Take a fresh, unlined white sheet of paper. Sign clearly using a thick black pen. Avoid blue ink as it is often a cause for rejection in the final scrutiny.</li>
        <li><strong>Use Our IBPS Resizer Tool:</strong> Select the "IBPS Photo" or "IBPS Signature" preset in the tool at the top of this page. Upload your raw image.</li>
        <li><strong>Adjust and Crop:</strong> Drag the crop box so your face covers about 80% of the photo area. For signatures, ensure the entire text fits within the boundaries.</li>
        <li><strong>Download & Verify:</strong> The tool will automatically output a file sized exactly between 20-50KB (for photos) or 10-20KB (for signatures) with the correct 200x230 or 140x60 pixel dimensions.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 16px;">Common IBPS Image Upload Errors & Troubleshooting</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;">During peak exam cycles (usually between June and October when IBPS RRB, PO, and Clerk applications open), the server experiences heavy loads, and validation becomes extremely strict. If you encounter the dreaded <em>"File size is not valid"</em> or <em>"Invalid Image Dimensions"</em> errors, check the following:</p>
      
      <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
        <li><strong>The "Size Exceeded" Error:</strong> This happens when your image is even 50.1 KB. Our tool safely compresses files to ~35KB to give you a safe buffer below the maximum threshold.</li>
        <li><strong>The "Invalid Format" Error:</strong> The IBPS portal strictly only accepts <code>.jpg</code> and <code>.jpeg</code>. If you are trying to upload a <code>.png</code> or <code>.webp</code>, it will fail. The resizer above automatically converts your exports to compliant JPEG format.</li>
        <li><strong>Blurry Uploads:</strong> Extreme compression can make signatures unreadable. If your signature looks too pixelated at 10-20KB, ensure your original photo is taken close up and well-lit before resizing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 16px;">What Happens If Your Photo Is Rejected?</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
        If you upload an incorrect photo (e.g., wearing sunglasses, wrong background, or signature in block letters), the application portal might accept it initially, but your admit card could be withheld, or you could be disqualified at the exam center. In rare cases where IBPS allows a correction window, you will receive an SMS/Email to re-upload your photo. However, banking exams usually <strong>do not provide an edit window</strong> once the form is submitted and the fee is paid. This makes it critical to use an exact IBPS size converter on your first attempt.
      </p>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface-1); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-lime); padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 48px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;">
        <h4 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Don't Forget the Thumb Impression & Declaration</h4>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
          In addition to the photo and signature, IBPS requires a Left Thumb Impression (20KB - 50KB, Black/Blue ink on white paper) and a Handwritten Declaration (50KB - 100KB, Black ink on white paper, English only).
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 24px;">Frequently Asked Questions (IBPS Exams)</h3>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px;">
        <div>
          <h4 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">1. Can I wear spectacles in my IBPS photograph?</h4>
          <p style="margin: 0;">Yes, you can wear spectacles if you use them regularly for vision correction. However, ensure there are no reflections or glare on the lenses, and your eyes are fully visible. Dark glasses or tinted lenses are strictly prohibited.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">2. What if my signature is slightly above 20KB?</h4>
          <p style="margin: 0;">The IBPS upload portal will instantly reject any signature file that exceeds 20.0 KB. You must use a compression tool like ours to bring the file size down to the acceptable 10KB - 20KB range without making it illegible.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">3. Are the photo dimensions exactly 200x230 pixels mandatory?</h4>
          <p style="margin: 0;">While the notification mentions 200 x 230 pixels as "preferred", the portal is often rigid about these specific aspect ratios. It is highly recommended to stick to 200x230px to avoid unexpected stretching or distortion of your face on the final admit card.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">4. Does this tool work for SBI PO and RBI Assistant exams as well?</h4>
          <p style="margin: 0;">Yes! Most major banking recruitment bodies in India, including State Bank of India (SBI), Reserve Bank of India (RBI), and NABARD, follow the exact same TCS iON portal guidelines as IBPS (20-50KB for photos, 10-20KB for signatures).</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </article>

  </main>
</Layout>
